A||N||6||kornholio||BRAKE HELP PLEASE||||4||
Z||000000||kornholio||05-23-2001||06:42 PM||||Today I start up my car and step on the brake and it drops to the floor.  I check the fluid and it is half gone.  I filled it up but the same thing happens, the pedal feels spongy.  I pump it a couple times and it goes from normal to spongy.  I pumped the brakes for probably half an hour to see if any of the calipers were leaking.  I didn't see any leak.  The brake light also turned on a couple times.  Anyone know what these are symptoms are?  Thanks.||||reg||4
Z||000001||PBJ||05-23-2001||06:53 PM||||was either the frt or back portion of master cylinder reservoir completely empty?||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||05-23-2001||07:04 PM||||Both sides of the reservoir were at the half way mark.  I also noticed that the fluid that was left was a orangy colour.||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-23-2001||07:11 PM||||Since you still had fluid and no brake pedal and you didn't empty the resivior with all that pumping, I would say you have a bad master cylender.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kornholio||05-23-2001||07:14 PM||||if it's a bad master cylinder, how come my fluid level dropped half way.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||05-23-2001||07:36 PM||||Try bleeding the brakes. Couldn't hurt to do it anyway and if the master cylinder pumps the fluid through the system and out the bleeders then you know it works.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||05-23-2001||08:33 PM||||Check under the dash where the MC pushrod goes through the firewall to the MC.  It might be leaking from the piston.  See if the carpet feels wet from brake fluid.<P>I would also trace the hard brake lines from the proportioning valve to each caliper.  Also check the rubber brake lines at each caliper carefully.  <P>Unless the fluid has been 1/2 full for a long time, the fluid has gone somewhere.  If it was me I wouldn't drive the car until I discovered where it was going.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
